%% Title: Effective Execution Config Resolution And Artifact Hashing
%% @version 1.1.0
%% @date    2026-10-09
%% Reviewed against main 9a7339dc: runtime_builders/effective_config_artifact_builder.py; services/control_plane/effective_config/service.py, context.py and runtime_overrides.py
%% @type    sequenceDiagram
%% @level   System / Interaction
%% @nodes   9
%% RULES: RULES.md §2.6, §2.8, ADR-025, ADR-044
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Bootstrap as runtime assembly / resolved config inputs
    participant Builder as effective_config_artifact_builder
    participant Service as EffectiveConfigService
    participant Context as build_effective_config_context
    participant Overrides as build_effective_execution_config
    participant Hash as stable_json_hash
    participant Artifact as EffectiveConfigArtifact
    participant Hashes as EffectiveConfigHashes
    participant Store as effective config artifact store

    Bootstrap->>Builder: resolved config, runtime overrides, policy and source refs
    Builder->>Service: create_effective_config_artifact(...)
    Service->>Context: derive snapshots, DQ policy and provenance
    Context->>Overrides: apply runtime overrides to resolved config
    Overrides->>Hash: hash versioned effective config payload
    Hash-->>Overrides: effective_hash
    Overrides-->>Context: EffectiveExecutionConfig
    Context-->>Service: resolved / effective snapshots and provenance
    Service->>Artifact: construct with derived hashes and semantic identity
    Artifact-->>Builder: immutable artifact
    Builder->>Store: save(artifact_id, run_id, serialized payload)
    Store-->>Builder: persistence success (errors propagate)
    Builder-->>Bootstrap: artifact_id and provenance hash values
    opt separate hash projection requested
        Service->>Hashes: construct derived hash container from artifact
    end

    Note over Context,Artifact: RuntimeOverrideSnapshot and ExecutionEnvironmentSnapshot become durable provenance. EffectiveConfigHashes is not an owned artifact field.
